{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Now the serpent was cunning.</b> He attached the serpent to the woman because the satan was created with her, and she is the body of the evil impulse, and she is easily seduced. And so the numerical value of נח\"ש is equal to the numerical value of שטן with the addition of the article." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> R. Shmuel bar Nachmani said: They said to the serpent, 'Why are you found among fences?' He said to them, 'Because he breached the fence of the world.' 'And why do you walk with your tongue dripping?' He said to them, 'Because he caused me.' 'And why does every beast bite and not kill, while you bite and kill, as it says (Ecclesiastes 10:11) ״אם ישך הנחש בלוא לחש ואין יתרון לבעל הלשון״?' He said to them, 'Is it possible? I am a servant — could I do anything, and it not be reported Above?' 'And why do you bite in one limb and all the limbs feel it?' He said to them, 'And is it to me that you say this? Say it to the slanderer who is here and kills in Rome!'" "<b>Although Elohim said.</b> The beginning of the serpent's speech was אף. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: four began with אף and were lost from the world, and these are they: the serpent, the chief cupbearer, the assembly of Korah, and Haman. The serpent — אף כי אמר אלהים. The chief cupbearer — (Genesis 40:16) אף אני בחלומי. The assembly of Korah — (Numbers 16:14) אף לא אל ארץ זבת חלב ודבש. Haman — (Esther 5:12) אף לא הביאה אסתר."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "The midrashic dialogue contains Aramaic phrases preserved as quoted; rendered literally without smoothing. The final exchange alludes to the slanderer/talebearer of Ecclesiastes 10:11 being identified with a power active in Rome."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:09:40.238810947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}